New algorithm: For each bin, compute the remaining capacity after hypothetically adding the item, then assign higher priority to bins where the remaining capacity is minimized (closest to zero without going negative), and among those, break ties by preferring bins with larger current capacity.
}

{
New algorithm: For each bin, compute the ratio of the item size to the bin capacity, then assign higher priority to bins where this ratio is closest to 1 (item fits perfectly), but penalize bins where the item exceeds capacity.
}

{
New algorithm: For each bin, compute the ratio of the item size to the bin's remaining capacity, then assign higher priority to bins where this ratio is larger (more fully filled), and among those, break ties by preferring bins with larger current capacity.
}

{
New algorithm: Prioritize bins where the item fits by maximizing the post-placement fill ratio, while applying a penalty for bins where the item does not fit, and using a power-law scaling on the remaining space to favor nearly-full bins.
